            "review_text": "rachel_moran1006\nLondon, United Kingdom117 contributions\n0\nGood vegetarian food on a budget\nMar 2019 • Solo\nCame here twice (one dinner, one lunch) because it was close to my hostel. The food is cheap and filling with large portions. There were many locals eating, which is always a good sign. They have daily dinner specials but unfortunately they'd run out of that day's when I was there. I had the Bun Hue for 40,000 VND and it was perfectly nice. The next day I had lunch, a tasty and simple mixed vegetable noodle soup. I would definitely go back if I was in Ho Chi Minh again.\nRead more\nWritten March 17, 2019",
