            "review_text": "hangontravelingwoman\nMinato, Japan521 contributions\n0\nHit or miss service\nMar 2017 • Couples\nMy husband and I visited Dinh Y on our last night in HCMC. \n\nWe ordered 4 dishes. Stir fried veggies, soup, fried rice and deep fried tofu. \n\nThey took so long to bring the tofu out my husband asked if we could cancel it as it was becoming obvious that we were going to finish our meal before it came out. \n\nThe waiter said \"yes ok cancel\" and 1 minute later brought it out saying \"already made\". Since we had ordered it we tried to eat it but the batter it was fried in was drenched in chili and it was so spicy it was impossible to eat. My husband and I could only eat one piece each. \n\nIt would be helpful if they could write on the menu which dishes are spicy since most of the staff don't speak English. \n\nI had assumed it was mild since it's tofu and the menu didn't say spicy fried tofu. \n\nWhen we tried to get the attention of the waiters to order and then to cancel that one tofu dish they kept on going to get the one and only waiter who seemed to speak English so he was rushed off his feet. \n\nThey either need to hire more English speakers or add some additional information to the menu. \n\nWe were not the only ones who had problems. A couple sitting on the table opposite us had ordered but the waiter went to the table to say \"sorry we don't have your order it's lost, can you order again?\" He went over several more times,something was brought to their table which wasn't what they ordered and eventually they got SOME of their order. \n\nIt's true that this place is cheap but the service is seriously haphazard.\nRead more\nWritten March 28, 2017",
